Advanced static numerical-field verification (@em-static-numerics-study: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @electromagnetism, #source "../sources/Classical-Electromagnetism-Fitzpatrick.lingua#r_7NH7AZZH3NZ2FHJ4K5VBT49F6H", #source "../sources/Electromagnetics-Volume-1-Ellingson.lingua#r_30KS80JAJY91W0FGZMASQW9DJA", #electromagnetism "../study/An-integrated-electromagnetic-system-investigation.lingua#r_1FQW2ASX2WCT3JRXKKP4NB4HSN") { r_0HV1EN0TSCEJ133D4S253Z0PXD
**Read:** [Classical Electromagnetism — Richard Fitzpatrick](../sources/Classical-Electromagnetism-Fitzpatrick.lingua#r_7NH7AZZH3NZ2FHJ4K5VBT49F6H), whole relevant potential and boundary methods; [Electromagnetics Volume 1 — Steven W. Ellingson](../sources/Electromagnetics-Volume-1-Ellingson.lingua#r_30KS80JAJY91W0FGZMASQW9DJA), complete electrostatic/interface chapters.

Begin with the original conservative one-dimensional electrostatic solver and its exact interface/series-capacitance limits. Read the complete applicable boundary and numerical methods from [Classical Electromagnetism — Richard Fitzpatrick](../sources/Classical-Electromagnetism-Fitzpatrick.lingua#r_7NH7AZZH3NZ2FHJ4K5VBT49F6H) and [Electromagnetics Volume 1 — Steven W. Ellingson](../sources/Electromagnetics-Volume-1-Ellingson.lingua#r_30KS80JAJY91W0FGZMASQW9DJA). Derive a two-dimensional finite-volume or finite-element problem with actual interface conditions and an analytical/manufactured reference.

Implement or use an authorized external solver with a pinned version and reconstruct the discrete weak/balance equations. Compare an independent discretization or Green-function solution. Check local residuals, global charge, energy, reciprocity and forces. Include positive-permittivity conditioning, a nonuniform mesh and a singular corner/source case with an explicitly defined observable.

Perform at least three useful refinements, separate algebraic tolerance from spatial and domain errors, and compare the observed order with the theory's assumptions. Show a deliberately plausible but incorrect face/material averaging scheme and explain the conservation or interface error it creates. Carry a geometry/material uncertainty through to a physical claim. A verified small implementation should support a larger field investigation while preserving its stated scope; it does not establish that every future mesh or nonlinear model is correct.

**Continue:** [An integrated electromagnetic-system investigation](../study/An-integrated-electromagnetic-system-investigation.lingua#r_1FQW2ASX2WCT3JRXKKP4NB4HSN).

**Return:** [Electromagnetism — charge, fields, matter, waves and physical evidence](../Electromagnetism.lingua#r_5TJPESCTTNAKY66JH2QNQYN1PY).
